For polynomial h, Q and inverse-polynomial δ, Construction 6.4 achieves the following soundness parameter against any Q-query adversary [arXiv:2609.38945, p.18]:

β′(λ) = e^{−Ω(√max{λ, h(λ)^{2/c}})}

This simplifies in steps [arXiv:2609.38945, p.18]:

- β′(λ) ≤ e^{−Ω(√(√λ · √(h(λ)^{2/c})))}
- = e^{−Ω(λ^{1/4} · h(λ)^{1/(2c)})}
- ≤ e^{−Ω(λ^{1/4} · h(λ))}
- = (e^{−Ω(λ^{1/4})})^{h(λ)}

The last two steps use c ∈ (0, 1/2), which makes 1/(2c) > 1 [arXiv:2609.38945, p.18]. The final bound is exponentially small in h(λ).
